# Review: DoctorPlugin

The `queryComposerLogs` operation is fully built: the schema in `DoctorOperation.ts` matches the spec's input
and output, the handler reads the IndexedDB store through `readLogRows`, and the pure engine `runQuery` does
filtering, projection, grouping, aggregation and clamping. `log-query.test.ts` exercises the engine well, but
nothing tests the handler or the IndexedDB reader (the handler carries a TODO for an end-to-end test), and
nothing tests that the skill offers the tool. The one real divergence is in F-1.9: when the handler exits the
cursor early at `limit`, `runQuery` sees exactly `limit` rows and reports `truncated: false` even when the store
has more. The plugin also ships a diagnostics panel and providers that the spec does not describe.

Of 13 items: 9 done, 1 untested, 2 partial, 0 diverged, 1 missing.

