verdict F-1.9: Caps are clamped, but the early-exit read path loses the truncated flag.
  status: partial
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-doctor/src/operations/internal/log-query.ts#clampLimit, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-doctor/src/operations/internal/log-query.ts#clampTopK, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-doctor/src/operations/internal/log-query.ts#clampSampleSize, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-doctor/src/operations/query-composer-logs.ts]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-doctor/src/operations/internal/log-query.test.ts]
  note: |
    `runQuery` clamps to 1000/1000/25 and sets `truncated` when it drops rows or groups. But for an unfiltered
    query the handler stops the cursor once it has `limit` rows, so `runQuery` never sees the rest and returns
    `truncated: false` although the store had more. No test exercises the hard caps themselves.
```

